diff --git a/docs/architecture.md b/docs/architecture.md
index a1ae5c6..2d3176a 100644
--- a/docs/architecture.md
+++ b/docs/architecture.md
@@ -301,6 +301,13 @@ When an agent chat is selected in command mode, `/` focuses the chat, seeds the
 `/`, and enters insert mode so `/status`-style input submits through the same selected-agent chat
 path.
 
+Command mode supports Vim-style visual selection without adding a public `UiMode` variant. `v`, `V`,
+and `Ctrl-V` start characterwise, linewise, and blockwise selection in the focused pane. Arrow keys
+and `h/j/k/l` extend the selection, `y` yanks the selected text, `Y` yanks linewise text, and `Esc`
+cancels selection. The left-pane selection model uses the rendered control rows, including wrapped
+agent rows, while the right-pane model uses the rendered transcript text. Yanked text is queued for
+terminal clipboard output and the status line reports the copied character count.
+
 The terminal app maps a session to a left-pane `READY` marker when the controller exposes no loading
 state for that session. `TerminalUi` queues one terminal bell when a chat transitions into the ready
 state and renders ready rows in reverse video so they remain highlighted until the chat becomes busy
